        {
          "_key": "k4",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "OG images are one of the open graph protocols that enables any web page to become a rich object in a social graph. It is used to represent the page\nwhen shared on social media platforms like Facebook, Twitter, LinkedIn, etc."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "k5",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "k6",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Any webpage can be turned into graph objects by adding some of the basic meta tags to the page. The four required properties for every page are:"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "k7",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
